# What the build context does NOT need.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . /build/app` for the application's own modules,
# so everything not excluded here is uploaded to the daemon on every build.
# The measured effect of this file is in `docs/DEPLOY.md`: the context drops
# from megabytes to kilobytes, which is most of the difference between a
# `docker build` that starts instantly and one that pauses first.

.git
.github

# Build outputs and anything already compiled for THIS machine. `pq_native.so`
# is the sharp one: it is a glibc x86-64 shared object built by src/build.sh,
# and copying it into a musl builder would put a silently unloadable .so where
# something might later look for it.
*.so
*.o
*.a
akkar-app

# Test and benchmark machinery. `bench/` is deliberately Linux-only shell that
# expects docker, sudo and a reserved machine -- the rockspec already drops it
# from an installed rock for the same reason.
spec
bench
.busted

# Documentation. `docs/DEPLOY.md` describes this image; it does not belong
# inside it.
docs
README.md
LICENSE
types

# Scratch files from verification runs.
.dbtest.lua
.migtest.lua

# Local editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
